            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> Note that running the test case direct from nvim in a floating window is not as appealing to me, as I like to have the output in another terminal tab so I can refer to current output as well as previous outputs.\r\n\r\nIndeed, the currently suggested approach is to use [`run_at_location()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c32c6642f4b191138673a37dcc221c9e9afbbd38/doc/mini-test.txt#L380). I find that when mapped (for example, `<Leader>tl` for me) it provides a very streamlined workflow. If you want to inspect the output later, you can copy and paste in a scratch buffer.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it, but at the moment I don't think adding this functionality will be a good idea.",
